I now have enough information to write the Round 6 review. Let me synthesize my findings.

**Key verified facts:**
1. WikiMixQA (arXiv:2506.15594, ACL 2025 Findings) **confirmed**: The 14–27% scores ARE the oracle/direct-context scores — WebFetch of the actual paper confirms this. The Round 5 reviewer's claim that "the 27% figure was for the retrieval setting" was incorrect. Round 6 has this right.
2. WikiMixQA oracle format: table provided as **HTML** + chart as **separate image** — NOT a combined page image. LHEC cannot run DocLayout-YOLO on these separate inputs; the proposal never addresses this inference-time format difference.
3. Open-source model performance on WikiMixQA oracle is near-random (23–27% vs 25% random baseline), and barely scales from 1B to 78B — suggesting a fundamental cross-modal reasoning issue, not just a layout traversal issue.
4. LayoutLLM (arXiv:2404.05225, CVPR 2024) and DocLayLLM (arXiv:2408.15045, CVPR 2025) are now cited and differentiated — Round 5 Fix 1 resolved.
5. Qwen3-VL-8B confirmed released October 15, 2025, with the correct model family structure.
6. No concurrent work specifically trains generative VLMs on typed spatial document graph traversal with node-ID notation.

